Source
------
PubChem BioAssay (https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/), deposited by the
NCATS/NIEHS/EPA/FDA Tox21 programme, retrieved 2026-09-06 via the PUG-REST
concise assay endpoint:

  AID 743202 — "qHTS assay for small molecule agonists of the antioxidant
               response element (ARE) signaling pathway"
  AID 743203 — the same assay's cell viability counter screen, over the same
               library

The viability pool also uses PubChem AIDs 743086, 720693, 743209, 651633 and
1346977. The additional ARE training table comes from the United States EPA
invitrodb v4.3 AEID 1110 PubChem export of 18 August 2026 and its archived
2018 ToxCast chemical identity SDF:

  https://clowder.edap-cluster.com/api/files/6a85a260e4b0731a36bd04cc
  https://clowder.edap-cluster.com/api/files/6114f600e4b0856fdc65865c

Derivation
----------
Rows each assay called Active or Inactive were kept and rows it called
Inconclusive were dropped; compound identifiers were resolved to isomeric
SMILES through the PubChem compound property endpoint; structures were
standardised (normalise, largest fragment, neutralise) and collapsed to one row
per InChIKey by majority call, with ties dropped. Only the InChIKey,
standardised SMILES, the two binary labels, median reported potency and record
counts are retained.

For the EPA table, only Active and Inactive calls with resolved structures are
kept. Replicate calls are collapsed by majority, ties are dropped, and primary
screen identities and conflicting stereo duplicates are removed.

